{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetJ2he7KDWmuPDBJVFzX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n- Shipment entity: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:9-27` with status enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentController: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentController.kt:26-56` uses ResourceNotFoundException (404) and ConflictException (409)\n- ShipmentRepository: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:15-26` with findById, save\n- ApiExceptions: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt` defines ResourceNotFoundException and ConflictException\n- ErrorCode enum: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37` has SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND and SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS\n- GlobalExceptionHandler: `sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/GlobalExceptionHandler.kt:16-28` converts ApiException to ApiError envelope\n\n**Conventions:**\n- Endpoints return the full entity on success\n- Error responses use consistent ApiError envelope with code, message, fields\n- Controllers throw ApiException subclasses (ResourceNotFoundException for 404, ConflictException for 409)\n- These are handled globally and converted to JSON responses\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions for both status and response body\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `ApiError.kt` - Add error code for invalid state transition\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` - Add confirm endpoint\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Add tests for all confirm cases\n\n**Risks:**\n- Breaking existing tests if error codes or exception handling changes\n- Incorrect idempotency behavior for already-CONFIRMED shipments\n- Not returning correct status for CANCELLED shipments\n\n**Open questions:** None - the ticket is clear on all cases.\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt** — Add error code `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE` to the ErrorCode enum. This will be used when trying to confirm a shipment that is already CONFIRMED or CANCELLED.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt** — Add new `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` endpoint that:\n   - Retrieves the shipment by ID (404 if not found)\n   - If status is CREATED: updates to CONFIRMED, saves, and returns the updated shipment (200)\n   - If status is CONFIRMED: returns the shipment as-is (200, idempotent)\n   - If status is CANCELLED: throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE (409)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Add four new tests:\n   - Test confirming a CREATED shipment moves it to CONFIRMED\n   - Test confirming an already-CONFIRMED shipment succeeds (idempotent)\n   - Test confirming a CANCELLED shipment returns 409 with error code\n   - Test confirming a non-existent shipment returns 404 with error code\n\n**Alternatives considered:**\n\n1. **Add a separate service layer** — Could add a ShipmentService to encapsulate confirm logic, but this is overkill for a single state transition. The other endpoints (create, read) are simple enough that a controller-level implementation is consistent with existing patterns.\n\n2. **Use HTTP 204 No Content** — Could return 204 when confirming an already-CONFIRMED shipment, but the requirement says \"returns the shipment,\" implying 200 with body.\n\n3. **Add multiple error codes** (e.g., SHIPMENT_ALREADY_CONFIRMED, SHIPMENT_CANCELLED) — Could be more specific, but SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE is sufficient and simpler.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n- **Case 1: Confirming a CREATED shipment**\n  - Read: Find shipment by ID\n  - Write: Update status to CONFIRMED, save to repository\n  - Response: 200 with updated shipment entity\n  - Mechanism: `repository.findById()` → check status → `repository.save(shipment.copy(status = CONFIRMED))`\n\n- **Case 2: Confirming an already-CONFIRMED shipment**\n  - Read: Find shipment by ID\n  - Write: None (idempotent)\n  - Response: 200 with shipment entity unchanged\n  - Mechanism: `repository.findById()` → check status → return as-is\n\n- **Case 3: Confirming a CANCELLED shipment**\n  - Read: Find shipment by ID\n  - Write: None\n  - Response: 409 Conflict with error envelope (code: SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE)\n  - Mechanism: `repository.findById()` → check status → throw ConflictException\n\n- **Case 4: Confirming a non-existent shipment**\n  - Read: Find shipment by ID (returns null)\n  - Write: None\n  - Response: 404 Not Found with error envelope (code: SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND)\n  - Mechanism: `repository.findById()` → null → throw ResourceNotFoundException\n\n**Test strategy:**\n1. `confirms a CREATED shipment to CONFIRMED` — Create shipment, confirm it, verify status is CONFIRMED and response is 200\n2. `confirms an already CONFIRMED shipment idempotently` — Create and confirm shipment, confirm again, verify status is still CONFIRMED and response is 200\n3. `rejects confirming a CANCELLED shipment with 409` — Create shipment, manually set to CANCELLED in repository, attempt confirm, verify 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATE\n4. `rejects confirming a non-existent shipment with 404` — Attempt confirm on missing ID, verify 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1226,"cache_read_input_tokens":18326,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1226},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15d78560-ef4c-402d-b3a5-39521187913c","uuid":"1dff8879-479f-419f-9fd3-2b0cd4f8bebe","timestamp":"2026-09-09T17:54:57.011Z","request_id":"req_011CetJ2gxfux3dKRTf